{
  "dom_id": "step-q162555",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Given the vector field $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i+2xy\\,j,$ which of the following statements must be true?\n\nI. $∇\\cdot F\\ne 0$\n\nII. There exists a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ for $F$\n\nIII. $F$ is a source-free vector field",
  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field with simply connected domain $D⊆{R}^{2},$ then the following are equivalent:\n\n- $F$ is a source-free vector field.\n\n- $∇\\cdot F=\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=0.$\n\n- The flux ${∮}_{C}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s$ along any closed curve $C⊂D$ is zero.\n\n- Flux is path-independent. That is, given any two curves ${C}_{1},{C}_{2}⊂D$ with the same start and endpoints, we have that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{1}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{2}}F\\cdot n\\,\\text{d}s.\n$$\n\n- There exists a stream function $ψ(x,y)$ for $F.$\n\nNote that $F(x,y)={x}^{2}\\,i+2xy\\,j$ is a vector field with the simply connected domain $D={R}^{2},$ where $P(x,y)={x}^{2}$ and $Q(x,y)=2xy.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂P}{∂x}=2x,\\,\\frac{∂Q}{∂y} & =2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement.\n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, we have that\n\n$$\n\\frac{∂P}{∂x}+\\frac{∂Q}{∂y}=2x+2x=4x\\ne 0.\n$$\n\n- Statements II and III are false. Indeed, this follows from statement I.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
